# PHASE 6: SECURE CUSTOMER REGISTRATION AND DATABASE MANAGEMENT

Inspect the existing customer database schema before modifying it.

Implement registration using the existing data model where appropriate.

Required customer fields should include:

- Customer ID.
- Full Name.
- Email.
- Password Hash for password-based accounts.
- OAuth provider information where applicable.
- Account status.
- Created At.
- Updated At.

Do not require a phone number for customer registration.

For Google/Facebook accounts, support provider-linked authentication without requiring an unnecessary local password.

## Security Requirements

- Hash passwords using a secure password hashing algorithm such as Argon2id or appropriately configured bcrypt.
- Never store plaintext passwords.
- Enforce email uniqueness.
- Normalize email addresses consistently.
- Prevent duplicate account creation.
- Validate email and password server-side.
- Use secure session or token management.
- Implement proper session expiration.
- Protect against brute-force login attempts.
- Apply authentication rate limits.
- Prevent account enumeration where appropriate.
- Validate all request payloads.
- Never allow users to submit their own admin role.
- Never trust frontend authentication state as authorization proof.

If an existing email belongs to a password account, do not automatically link an OAuth identity solely because the provider returns a matching email unless the provider identity and email are sufficiently verified and the linking policy is secure.

Preserve existing customers and their order history.

Do not delete existing user records.

